From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:17:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] qwen3_5 CUDA: execute a looped checkpoint's plan and
 its two-stream mHC

A Qwen3.5 tower can declare a shared-weight loop (layers [4,28) run twice: 56
executions from 32 sets of weights) and manifold-constrained hyper-connections
over that range. The geometry derives the plan from loop_settings, sizes the KV
and recurrent caches by executions rather than physical layers (14 and 42 for
this model) and validates that the mHC window cannot cross a loop phase.

The forward iterates executions, so the delta/attention ordinals it already keeps
become the per-visit cache slots, and carries the residual in two streams between
the mHC boundaries: the window's first execution folds the previous layer's
pending output in, each boundary reads a branch of the streams and merges it back
through the Sinkhorn-normalised 2x2 map, and its last execution collapses the
streams' mean back into h.

Kernels: tf_q35_mhc_{branch,merge,enter,leave}. Weights: the routers stay fp32
and dt_bias accepts an HF checkpoint's f32.
